{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"answers\":[{\"question_id\":\"Q015_artifact_tag_not_homology\",\"answer\":\"In SCOPe 2.08, d1a14h1 (1a14 chain H residues 9–111) is the genuine immunoglobulin heavy-chain variable domain, classified in the V-set family b.1.1.1. The second segment, d1a14h2 (residues 1–8), is a synthetic N-terminal tag in artifact class l, under the Tags fold, superfamily, and family (l.1.1.1). Those artifact bins are descriptive, not evolutionary groupings: similarity confined to d1a14h2 does not support protein homology and must not justify transferring function or a biological SCOPe classification. It should be masked or excluded when selecting homologs, templates, or representatives; any biological relationship must instead be supported by independent sequence or structural evidence in the genuine protein region, such as d1a14h1.\",\"evidence_used\":[\"mcp__scope__get_scop_domains — /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1a14h1; /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1a14h1/parents; /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1a14h2; /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1a14h2/parents; /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1a14h2/homology\"]}]}"}}
